course: dictionary
lesson: 5131
title: Investigate: finding out the facts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To investigate means to look carefully to find out the facts about something. The words around it give you clues. «Elephants investigate new things carefully with their trunks» tells you the elephant touches and sniffs something new to learn about it. So investigate must mean to study something carefully to learn about it.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Elephants study new things carefully with their trunks» still makes sense, so your meaning fits. Always test your guess this way.
explain: The word is also used for finding the facts about a crime or problem. In the news, «the UN and international courts are investigating war crimes there» means they are looking carefully for the facts about what happened.
fact: Investigate means to try to find out the facts about something, especially a crime or problem.
fact: In science and maths, to investigate means to study or test something carefully to learn about it.
fact: «Elephants investigate new things carefully with their trunks» means they examine new things closely.
fact: A science investigation has steps: plan a fair test, collect results, then draw a conclusion.
fact: Forms of the word: investigate, investigates, investigated, investigating. Phrases: investigate further, investigate a crime.
exercise: «Elephants investigate new things carefully with their trunks.» What does investigate mean here? | *Study something carefully to learn about it | Make a loud noise | Run away from it fast | Forget about it
exercise: Maya wants to investigate how temperature affects melting. What should she do first? | Eat the ice | *Plan a fair test | Guess the answer and stop | Hide the results
exercise: Find and copy one word that is a form of investigate: «The detectives investigated the strange footprints and then looked further.» | *investigated | footprints | detectives | strange
test: Which phrase means to look into a crime to find the facts? | Forget the crime | Eat a big cake | *Investigate a crime | Paint a picture
test: Yesterday the police ____ the broken window to find out who did it. Which word fits best? | *investigated | investigating | investigates | investigate
exam: The scientists want to ____ whether plants grow faster in sunlight. Which word fits best? | sing | shout | *investigate | forget
